# Required for a physical device, in addition to .env: forces the Metro/
# Expo CLI dev server itself to advertise this same address for its own
# manifest/bundle URL (`expo start` otherwise auto-detects a LAN
# interface, wrong on a machine with more than one -- Tailscale, a real
# LAN adapter, and a Hyper-V/WSL virtual adapter can all show up as
# candidates). Same host as EXPO_PUBLIC_HTTP_URL in .env, no port.
#
# Has to live in a .local file, not .env -- Expo's own env loader
# hard-refuses to start with a non-EXPO_PUBLIC_ variable anywhere else
# ("Refused to load personal environment variables from a non-.local env
# file"), confirmed live. Verified this is the variable that actually
# works (not EXPO_PACKAGER_PROXY_URL, which looks like the documented
# answer for this and does nothing in practice) against a real Metro
# manifest response, not assumed from docs.
REACT_NATIVE_PACKAGER_HOSTNAME=192.168.1.100
